Local modifications (2026-11-20):
- src/term/mod.rs: opt-in Config.combining_limit, checked on the library's
  chosen target cell before appending each additional zero-width scalar.
- src/event.rs: typed CombiningLimitExceeded event for rejected input.
  RSQL treats this event as fatal. The default combining limit remains disabled.
- src/term/mod.rs and src/selection.rs route selections through grid reflow.
  src/selection/reflow.rs maps anchor sides and clips removed endpoints.
  Removed row suffixes stay distinguishable from retained endpoint cells.
  Word/line selections retain cropped bounds separately from their directed
  gesture anchors. Row erasure intersects an active extent. An intact resize
  leaves matching native word/line bounds live across character edits.
  src/selection/rotation.rs moves the anchors and surviving bounds through
  the scroll region and history. It resolves live word/line bounds before
  rows move and retains the mapped range if it splits, loses cells, or new
  neighbors change the native expansion. A gesture update re-expands from
  the fixed anchor.
  Block selection uses ordered cell edges for its half-open column interval.
  Copying a selected wrap placeholder reads the following wide cluster.
- src/term/cell.rs and src/term/mod.rs mark horizontal-tab padding in a cell
  flag during tab motion. Copy suppresses that padding across soft wraps when
  the tab itself is in the selection.
- src/term/selection_text.rs shares native selection extraction with a byte-limited copy
  path. It checks one native row at a time before appending to the result.
- src/grid/mod.rs, src/grid/resize.rs and src/grid/reflow.rs track selection
  coordinates (up to four for word/line gestures) through the existing row moves and history limit.

- src/term/cell_edit.rs and src/term/mod.rs preserve paired wide cells and the
  physical wrap margin across column insert, delete and erase. Deletes stay
  inside the cursor suffix. Rendering and extraction validate the wide lead.
- src/grid/row.rs gives published row contents an opaque, lazily assigned
  identity. Row moves preserve it. Edits, reuse and clones invalidate it.
  src/grid/storage.rs swaps the complete row independent of its layout.

All other distributed Rust source bytes match the published archive.
